      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "QtozjlDCbV_jAHsRHphfZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1852.747079454112,
      "y": 375.3026531797103,
      "width": 545.9100213443439,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1580393894,
      "version": 1062,
      "versionNonce": 151070566,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776802299300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When we use an LLM to compare values, what happens\nwhen we compare different kinds of language?\n\nCL expected value with CL actual value - LLM not\nnecessary to compare, just need to make sure files are\nformatted the same (\"Monday\" = \"Monday\"). Essentially\nperfect judgment of equality.\n\nCL expected value with NL actual value - actual value\nneeds to be converted into CL to be compared to\nexpected value using traditional logic\n\nNL expected value with CL actual value - is there ever\na situation where this would be necessary?\n\nNL expected value with NL actual value - can be sent\nto LLM together for comparison, but leaves room for\nerror by LLM. Weak judgment.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When we use an LLM to compare values, what happens when we compare different kinds of language?\n\nCL expected value with CL actual value - LLM not necessary to compare, just need to make sure files are formatted the same (\"Monday\" = \"Monday\"). Essentially perfect judgment of equality.\n\nCL expected value with NL actual value - actual value needs to be converted into CL to be compared to expected value using traditional logic\n\nNL expected value with CL actual value - is there ever a situation where this would be necessary?\n\nNL expected value with NL actual value - can be sent to LLM together for comparison, but leaves room for error by LLM. Weak judgment.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
